# Build & Install Workflow

## User shorthand

| Shorthand | Meaning | Agent action |
|-----------|---------|--------------|
| **bi** | build + install | `app\build-APK.bat install` |
| **bi-os** / **bios** | iOS build + TestFlight submit | `app\bi-os.bat` (loads ASC API key; no `--auto-submit`) |
| **build** / compile check | release APK only | `app\build-APK.bat` |
| **build ios** | iOS EAS build only | `app\build-ios.bat` |
| **submit ios** | Upload latest iOS build to TestFlight | `app\submit-ios.bat` |
| **cpd** | commit + push + deploy | Stage, commit, push & deploy to VPS (`ssh healthings-api "cd /opt/healthings-api && git pull && bash server/scripts/deploy-website.sh"`) |

Treat **bi**, **build install**, and **build and install** as equivalent.

Treat **bi-os** and **bios** as equivalent (iOS TestFlight pipeline).

Treat **cpd** and **commit push deploy** as equivalent (web/backend VPS deploy).

## Canonical build script — always use this

**Do not** run raw `gradlew` from the agent unless `build-APK.bat` is unavailable.
**Do not** pipe Gradle output to `Select-Object -Last N` or `Select-String` when the
user is waiting — that hides progress and looks frozen.

```
app\build-APK.bat           REM build only — live log
app\build-APK.bat install   REM build + adb install (bi)
```

`build-APK.bat` **always** sets `GRADLE_USER_HOME=C:\gradle-hm` (short path — avoids
Windows 260-char CMake/ninja failures), checks JDK via `check-java-for-android.bat`,
and passes `--console=plain` so Gradle streams task lines immediately.

## GRADLE_USER_HOME — required on Windows (especially agents)

**Recurring failure:** Cursor sandbox (and some shells) pre-set `GRADLE_USER_HOME` to a
long temp path (`…\cursor-sandbox-cache\…\gradle\…`). Native modules then fail with:

```
ninja: error: Stat(…/libreactnative.so): Filename longer than 260 characters
```

**Fix:** this repo **always** uses `C:\gradle-hm` — never the sandbox default.

| Who | What to do |
|-----|------------|
| **Agent** | Prefer `app\build-APK.bat` (forces short path). If build still hits 260-char ninja, prefix: `$env:GRADLE_USER_HOME = "C:\gradle-hm"` then re-run. **Do not** retry the same long-path build blindly. |
| **Raw gradlew** | Set `$env:GRADLE_USER_HOME = "C:\gradle-hm"` **before** any `gradlew.bat` call. |
| **User terminal** | `build-APK.bat` / `build-dev.bat` set it for you. |

Create the folder once if missing: `mkdir C:\gradle-hm` (Gradle creates caches inside).

| Script | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| **`build-APK.bat`** | Release APK for phone testing (this workflow) |
| **`build-dev.bat`** | Debug dev client + Metro — daily JS work, not release |
| **`build-release.bat`** | Legacy; prefer `build-APK.bat` |
| **`publish-apk-vps.bat`** | Build (if needed) + upload APK to VPS |

## Default behaviour after code changes

**Build for compilation check only** — do not install unless the user asks.

```
app\build-APK.bat
```

Install only when user says **bi** / install / test on phone:

```
app\build-APK.bat install
```

## When to install
- User explicitly says: "install", **"bi"**, "build install", "test on phone", "let me try it", "rebuild and install"
- After a bug fix the user reported from a device screenshot
- At the end of a feature batch when the user asks to verify

## When NOT to install automatically
- After every small fix (wastes 30–40 seconds per iteration)
- After a compilation-only change (import cleanup, type fix, dead code removal)
- When the user just asked to "rebuild" without mentioning the phone

## Commit policy — NEVER commit before phone test

**Do NOT `git commit` or `git push` after a feature build until the user explicitly
confirms they tested the APK on their phone and it works.**

Trigger words that mean "ok to commit":
- "commit", "push", "lgtm", "looks good", "works", "it's working", "ship it"

Trigger words that mean "NOT ok to commit yet":
- "build", "compile check", "let me test", "install" — wait for test result first

```
# ✅ Correct order
1. build-APK.bat  →  2. install (when asked)  →  3. User tests  →  4. User says "commit"  →  5. git commit & push

# ❌ Never do
Build APK  →  git commit  (skips phone test)
```

## Agent fallback (PowerShell — no && separator)

**First line is mandatory** — sandbox may already export a long `GRADLE_USER_HOME`.

If the batch file cannot be used, mirror its flags exactly:

```powershell
$env:GRADLE_USER_HOME = "C:\gradle-hm"
Set-Location "c:\projects\healthings-medilab\app\android"
.\gradlew.bat assembleRelease --no-build-cache --console=plain
```

Install (bi only):

```powershell
adb install -r "c:\projects\healthings-medilab\app\android\app\build\outputs\apk\release\app-release.apk"
```

Agent-only quick tail when user is **not** watching: last 12 lines is OK.

## Clean build (only when native modules / codegen errors)

```powershell
$env:GRADLE_USER_HOME = "C:\gradle-hm"
Set-Location "c:\projects\healthings-medilab\app\android"
.\gradlew.bat assembleRelease --no-build-cache --console=plain
```

Avoid `gradlew clean` unless codegen dirs are broken — see prior notes in `build-dev.bat`.

## iOS TestFlight (`bi-os`)

| Shorthand | Meaning | Agent action |
|-----------|---------|--------------|
| **bi-os** / **bios** | EAS build + submit to TestFlight | `app\bi-os.bat` |
| **build ios** | EAS build only | `app\build-ios.bat` |
| **submit ios** | Upload latest finished build | `app\submit-ios.bat` |

Treat **bi-os** and **bios** as equivalent.

### Canonical iOS script — always use this

**Do not** run `eas build --auto-submit` on Windows (Apple ID / SMS trap).

```
app\bi-os.bat    REM build on EAS cloud, then submit-ios (ASC API key)
```

`bi-os.bat` calls `app\scripts\bi-os.ps1`, which:

1. Loads `app\asc-api.local.ps1` if it exists (gitignored; copy from `asc-api.local.ps1.example`)
2. `eas build --platform ios --profile production` — wait until Finished on [expo.dev](https://expo.dev)
3. `eas submit --platform ios --profile production --latest --no-wait` — **never wait** for ASC/TestFlight processing; exit after schedule (Apple emails when ready)

At **“Do you want to log in to your Apple account?”** during build → answer **`n`** (use API key).

### Before each new TestFlight upload

Bump `ios.buildNumber` in `app/app.config.js` (and keep `version` aligned with Android).

### Split steps

```
app\build-ios.bat     REM compile-check equivalent — build only
app\submit-ios.bat    REM after build is Finished on expo.dev
```

Guide: `server/TESTFLIGHT-INTERNAL.md`

### Agent fallback (PowerShell)

If the batch file cannot be used:

```powershell
Set-Location "c:\projects\healthings-medilab\app"
& "c:\projects\healthings-medilab\app\scripts\bi-os.ps1"
```

Or manually mirror the two steps after dot-sourcing `asc-api.local.ps1`:

```powershell
eas build --platform ios --profile production
eas submit --platform ios --profile production --latest --no-wait
```

**Never** omit `--no-wait` on submit — do not block on App Store Connect / TestFlight processing.

### First-time setup (once per machine)

```powershell
npm install -g eas-cli
eas login
eas build:configure
```

Copy `asc-api.local.ps1.example` → `asc-api.local.ps1` and point `EXPO_ASC_API_KEY_PATH` at the `.p8` outside the repo.

### Default behaviour after iOS code changes

Run **`bi-os`** only when the user asks for TestFlight / iOS ship — not after every small JS tweak (EAS upload is slow).

Do **not** commit iOS release bumps until the user confirms TestFlight works (same policy as Android phone test).
